id: pm-kx6a8d
title: "Strict create takes a single --defer-reason, so a stdin-json round trip of deferrals with different reasons stores the joined reasons on every field"
description: "Follow-up from the PR #1725 review of pm-gh1713 (2026-11-14). deferred_fields stores one reason per field, but create accepts a single --defer-reason (SDK deferReason). When a pm get --json document with distinct per-field reasons is recreated through create --stdin-json, documentDeferralOptions joins the distinct reasons with '; ', and every recreated entry carries the joined text, so the original field-to-reason mapping is lost (the text itself is kept). Proposal: accept per-field reasons on create, for example --defer field=reason (SDK defer entries as {field, reason}), keep the shared --defer-reason as the default for bare field names, and make the stdin-json adapter emit per-field entries. Duplicate check: searched per-field deferral reason; no item."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 3
tags[4]: governance,importers,stdin-json,strict-preset
created_at: "2026-11-14T15:21:40.765Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-14T15:26:13.353Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "Create accepts per-field deferral reasons on the CLI, the SDK and MCP while a shared --defer-reason still applies to bare field names; A stdin-json round trip of deferrals with distinct reasons recreates each field with its own reason; Conflict and validation rules of pm-gh1713 are unchanged"
parent: pm-33cw
risk: low
confidence: high
expected_result: A recreated deferral keeps each field's own reason
actual_result: Every recreated field carries the joined reasons of all fields
